The Iron Man Mark XLII (42) suit serves as the hero armor of Iron Man 3, famously nicknamed the "Prodigal Son" for its revolutionary autonomous propulsion system. Driven by micro-repeated sub-dermal implants under Tony Stark's skin, individual pieces of the armor can fly long distances independently to attach piece-by-piece directly onto Tony's body, or even onto someone else to protect them. Sporting a distinct champagne-gold dominant color scheme with red accents, the prototype suit was designed for extreme flexibility and remote piloting via a specialized heads-up headset, though its experimental state meant it frequently suffered power drain issues and structural fragility—ultimately being detonated by Tony during the final battle against Aldrich Killian.
